  "rationale": "The sole supplied evidence (provider-player) is the Swagit player page on the City of Denton portal (dentontx.new.swagit.com) titling recording 14004 'League of Women Voters Candidate Forum - Denton, TX', dated Apr 18, 2018. The actual convened program is the League of Women Voters Candidate Forum, an event of a private civic organization, not a municipal body; per the identity rule the convened body governs, not venue, topic, or the city platform on which the video happens to be hosted. No supplied evidence proves any Denton municipal body convened or jointly participated, so no body feed may be assigned: denton-tx-city-council is barred because the series rule states candidate forums remain archival series, not Council proceedings, and denton-tx-public-info-meetings is unproven since no evidence shows the city convened this as a public information meeting and routine topic/venue matching does not create membership. The general series rule directly covers candidate forums, so publication_action is archive_series with empty feed_slugs; this empty list reflects the approved archival-series disposition, not a determination that the recording is a non-meeting. The forum is named in bodies only as the actual proven program from the immutable recording title; it is not being established as a municipal institution from a program label, and no feed slug was invented. If a municipal co-convener existed, the supplied record contains no proof of it, so no additional assignment is made."
